                <mxCell id="_5K4IyTiggNPLRhWUsHf-1069" value="&lt;strike&gt;I think my idea here is going to be to simply dispatch 8 pixels / cycle round robin style to all the SMs. Basically, ever SM will have its own fragment reservoir. This is what the dispatcher will fill up round robin style 8 fragments per cycle. This significantly reduces crossbar area and power, it&#39;s a major saving. Once the fragment reservoir is full, the SM can look for a free subcore. If it finds it, it will start working on the fragment. Of course, we will probably have to have 64 fragment large reservoirs 2 fully fill 2 threadblocks / 1 warp group worth for best utilization.&lt;/strike&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strike&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strike&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strike&gt;I don&#39;t really like this idea because it doesn&#39;t take advantage of consecutive serialized pixels being guaranteed, but adding real collection logic could tricky very fast. Need consult.&lt;/strike&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" parent="_5K4IyTiggNPLRhWUsHf-1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="6390" y="1692.1900000000003" width="360" height="200" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
