                <mxCell id="_5K4IyTiggNPLRhWUsHf-1115" value="Aa + Bb + Cc" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" parent="_5K4IyTiggNPLRhWUsHf-1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="5410" y="740" width="110" height="30" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="_5K4IyTiggNPLRhWUsHf-1116" value="Let there be an early Z cache in memory. That is what this cache writes to. So it basically becomes a scoreboard here for tracking how i am going to be packing warps without dependency issues. Coming out of edge test each fragment in quad will be labeled 0 1 2 3, then they will be packed into warps according to this. Warp full of 0s, warp full of 1s, etc. That will be sent out. This is done because there is no intra thread dependency for order for textures and derivative calculation. So we will make the inter warp dependency handle it for us. 0 1st, then 1, then 2. After tall this attribute interpolation is done, texture stuff can be done. Since all the data is there and calculatable and gettable it is not a problem, will be in dcache. This will be passed to TMU.&amp;nbsp;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" parent="_5K4IyTiggNPLRhWUsHf-1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="5955.04" y="678.0300000000001" width="370" height="189.92" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="_5K4IyTiggNPLRhWUsHf-1117" value="NEW IDEA! I will collect warps worth of quads to send out. I will send out a signal saying i want to send, once i get ack from TBS i will slowly start piping the data out. How to collect? Have 4 registers storing pixels. Use FSM to put them in one by one. It&#39;s slow but its fine." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" parent="_5K4IyTiggNPLRhWUsHf-1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="6355.04" y="1552.19" width="280" height="140" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
